   "derivation": "One run covering all 5 returns, so lowest = highest = the full-period correlation. X 1,2,3,2,1 (mean 1.8), Y 1,3,2,2,3 (mean 2.2), in %. Deviations X -0.8, 0.2, 1.2, 0.2, -0.8; Y -1.2, 0.8, -0.2, -0.2, 0.8. Sum of products 0.96 + 0.16 - 0.24 - 0.04 - 0.64 = 0.2. Sums of squares 2.8 and 2.8. Correlation = 0.2 / 2.8 = 1/14 = 0.0714."
