   "derivation": "Start Nov 2019 at 90/10 of 1: tracker 0.9, asset 0.1. Dec 2019: asset doubles to 0.2, total 1.1; it is December, so reset to 90/10: 0.99 and 0.11. Jan 2020: asset halves to 0.055, total 1.045. Flat after (the Dec 2020 reset changes nothing). Total +4.5% over 15 months; per year 1.045^(12/15) - 1. Without rebalancing the mix would end at 0.9 + 0.1 = 1.0 (0%); rebalancing on the anniversary (Nov 2020) would also give 0%, so this case catches the wrong rule or the wrong timing. Mix volatility: monthly returns +10%, -5%, then thirteen 0%; sample variance x 12 = 37/3500, volatility sqrt(37/3500). Mix largest fall: 1.1 to 1.045 = -5%, Dec 2019 to Jan 2020, not recovered by Feb 2021, 14 months underwater. The tracker is flat: 0% everywhere, no fall."
  },
